    ('p', 'The persona is a solo seller - a founder, an independent rep, or a consultant whose income depends on how well their calls go. Their week contains perhaps five to fifteen recorded conversations. Their pain is not volume; it is that every call evaporates the moment it ends. Notes are forgotten, objections recur unhandled, the same discovery questions go unasked for weeks, and nobody - least of all a manager, because there is none - ever replays the tape. AMBER exists to be that replay: a patient, private analyst that reads every call and never forgets any of them.'),
